<title>UK: SNOOKER-LATEST POSITIONS IN WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP.</title>
<headline>SNOOKER-LATEST POSITIONS IN WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP.</headline>
<dateline>SHEFFIELD, England 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results and latest</p>
<p>positions in the best-of-19-frames first round of the world</p>
<p>professional snooker championship on Friday</p>
<p>(prefix number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>12-James Wattana (Thailand) beat Graeme Dott (Scotland) 10-9</p>
<p>Dominic Dale (Wales) beat 15-Tony Drago (Malta) 10-9</p>
<p>Latest positions in the best of 25 frames second round.</p>
<p>9-Darren Morgan (Wales) leads 8-Ronnie O'Sullivan (England) 5-3</p>
<p>6-Alan McManus (Scotland) tied with Lee Walker (Wales) 4-4</p>
<p>16-Mark Williams (Wales) leads 1-Stephen Hendry (Scotland) 4-2</p>
</text>
